  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: Question1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: 1. What is the IUPAC name of acetanilide?
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'Acetanilide is formed by replacing one of the hydrogen atoms
    in the -NH2 group of aniline with the -

    COCH3 group. It is represented by
    the formula C&H5-NH-CO-CH3.

    Hence, it is an amide of 2 carbon atoms, but
    one of the substituents on the nitrogen is the phenyl (-

    C&H5) group. So,
    its IUPAC name is N-phenylethanamide.'
  options:
  - N-ethylbenzamide
  - Phenylamine
  - N-phenylethenamide
  - N-ethylaniline
  correctOptionIndex: 2
